## On the phone

Tap Start on Home's Today card. With an active split, today's day loads with its planned sets; otherwise you
start an empty workout. The exercise you're on is lifted out as a card; the ones you've finished fold to
one line with what you did, and the rest wait under Up next with their plan in blue. Tap any of them to
open it. Tap the circle on a set when you've done it: it fills in what was planned and starts your rest
timer in the bar at the bottom (−15, +15 or Skip), then asks how many more you could have done: one tap,
or ignore it. You can turn that off in Settings › Workout. Tap the line under an exercise's name ("+2 kg ·
A set goes up at 7 reps") to see why it planned that weight. Swipe a set left for its options (the kind
of set, reps left, rest after it, a note, move it or delete it), and hold its number to drag it. The ⋯ next
to an exercise swaps it (just today, or in your plan too), groups it into a superset or circuit, adds
warm-ups, sets its rest or machine, or removes it. Add to workout at the bottom finds exercises, cardio,
drills and plugin blocks, several at once. The ⋮ menu at the top has Undo, Redo, Change the order and
Discard workout. Tap Finish when you're done: you see what's planned for next time and what you skipped,
and progression works out your next targets from it. The chevron at the top left minimises the workout
to a bar above the nav, so you can look at anything else and come straight back. The tour the app shows on your first
workout:

